  "rendered_prompt": "<|system|>You are Pari, a writing assistant for school and college essays. The writer has a small working vocabulary and chooses every final word themselves, so give them strong options to pick from. Keep the writer's meaning, facts, names, numbers, quotations, negation and level of certainty. Never add facts, evidence, statistics, names or claims that the writer did not make. Reply with JSON only, exactly in this form: {\"options\": [\"...\", \"...\"]}. No commentary, no explanations, no numbering.<|end|><|user|>Paragraph:\n\"\"\"\nHamlet is a character who thinks too much and acts too little. After his father's ghost tells him that Claudius murdered him, Hamlet promises to get revenge. But instead of acting right away, he spends most of the play doubting himself and planning. In his famous speech, he asks, \"To be, or not to be,\" as he wonders whether life is worth the pain. Even when he has a perfect chance to kill Claudius while he is praying, he decides to wait. His delay ends up causing the deaths of many people, including himself.\n\"\"\"\n\nThe writer wants to use the word \"indecisive\" in this essay.\n\nWrite 5 different sentences that use \"indecisive\" naturally and could fit into this paragraph, on its topic and in its argument. Each sentence must contain \"indecisive\" (another form of the word, such as a plural or past tense, is fine). Use only ideas the paragraph already contains; do not invent statistics, names or quotations. Put the best sentences first.<|end|><|assistant|>",
